messages:
sara: Quick sync — PM asked for a compatibility plan for the upcoming API changes: function-calling, structured_output schema, and minor embeddings tweaks. Need SDK + docs alignment. Who can own?
noah: I can share customer asks: two mid-market customers (payments + search infra) need a stable TypeScript typing story and a clear Python migration guide. Target GA in ~6 weeks. Must include changelog + migration examples.
jordan: I can own the SDK side. High-level plan: 1) Add optional `tools` and `structured_output_schema` fields to the request objects. 2) Keep current call signatures backward-compatible (opt-in). 3) Bump TS minor, release Python patch with typing stubs. Thoughts?
tina: Docs needs launch criteria: sample end-to-end example (TS + Py), a migration guide showing old->new payloads, and a quick compat FAQ. Also need code snippets for function/tool calling + structured output. ETA for docs draft?
jordan: Proposal for TS types (draft):

```ts
type ChatRequest = {
  model: string;
  messages: Message[];
  tools?: ToolDefinition[]; // optional - opt-in
  structured_output_schema?: Record<string, any>;
}

type Message = { role: 'user' | 'system' | 'assistant'; content: string };
```

We will add discriminated unions for response types: { kind: 'text', text: string } | { kind: 'tool_call', tool_name: string, args: any } to keep exhaustive checks.
sara: Good. Make sure we document example error cases when tool_call missing handler (fallbacks). Customers care about predictable fallbacks.
jordan: For Python, plan is to keep runtime objects the same but ship updated typing .pyi stubs and add a `response.kind` enum. Example:

```py
resp = client.chat.create(...)
if resp.kind == 'tool_call':
    handle_tool(resp.tool_name, resp.args)
else:
    print(resp.text)
```

This keeps codepaths minimal and backwards compatible.
tina: Changelog format: one entry per SDK with sections: Breaking, Notable, Migration. For this change: Breaking = none (opt-in). Notable = new structured_output & tool-calling fields. Migration = small snippet.
sara: Scope negotiation: can we trim the first rollout to hosted API + TS SDK + docs, and delay full Python typing enforcement to week 3 so we don't block GA? Customers said TS is higher priority.
jordan: Yes, let's do staged rollout. Week 0: feature flags on hosted API + TS SDK PR (minor). Week 1: docs + examples. Week 2: gated Python typing PR + pypi release. Week 3: full GA and native examples.
noah: Approved. Add: add telemetry event names for telemetry team: chat.tool_called, chat.structured_output_matched.
sara: Action items:
- jordan: open TS PR with types + examples by EOD Tue (<https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk-js/pulls>)
- tina: draft docs (examples + migration) by Thu
- jordan: coordinate Python typing stubs, target soft freeze in 2 weeks
- noah: coordinate customer communications + canary test groups
- sara: add rollout checklist in product board

jordan: quick sample TS example to include in docs:

```ts
const res = await client.chat.create({
  model: 'rwk-large',
  messages: [{role: 'user', content: 'Calculate tax for $12000'}],
  tools: [{name: 'tax-calc', schema: {amount: 'number'}}],
  structured_output_schema: {total_tax: {type: 'number'}}
});

if (res.kind === 'tool_call') {
  // handle tool
}
```

tina: I'll add that to examples. Also want a small runnable notebook for Py to land in examples repo.
ci-bot: CI passed for js PR #432 — tests 312/312 green :white_check_mark:
sara: OK team, we want minimal churn for customers. Keep default behavior unchanged unless `tools` or `structured_output_schema` provided. We'll reconvene in 48h for status updates. :thumbsup:
